    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1223">

                <pb facs="1116" n="858" xml:id="pg858"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/1869</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Spring Rice</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In further reply to your
                    excellency’s note of the 9th instant, and supplementary to the Department’s
                    answer of the 13th instant,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1223-f1"/> I have the honor to
                    inform you that the fast German steamships now in the continental ports of the
                    United States have been thoroughly reexamined and searched by American
                    authorities, with a view to verifying the information reported in your
                    excellency’s note of March 9, and that the Department is now in receipt of the
                    results of this investigation. It is deemed unnecessary to review this report in
                    detail, inasmuch as the Government is satisfied from the information at hand
                    that it has fully carried out its duties and obligations as a neutral in respect
                    to vessels of belligerent nationality in its ports.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
